numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4]
doubled = map(numbers, number => number * 2)
large = filter(doubled, number => number > 4)
total = large.length

{doubled: doubled, large: large, total: total}
// Mini tutorial: callbacks.
// This example demonstrates core Discript syntax and runtime behavior.
// Run it with: discript examples/fundamentals/callbacks.ds (or pipe it to discript for stdin mode).
// Read the final value and comments together to follow the data flow.
/* Tutorial focus: This demonstrates arrow callbacks with `map` and `filter` to transform and select values. */
